======================================================================
THEOREM B: 2^{C(p,2)} ≡ (2/p) (mod p²)
  The labeled tournament count remembers the Legendre symbol
======================================================================

Proof sketch:
  2^{C(p,2)} = 2^{p(p-1)/2} = (2^{(p-1)/2})^p
  Case (2/p)=1: 2^{(p-1)/2} = 1+pa, so (1+pa)^p ≡ 1 (mod p²)
  Case (2/p)=-1: 2^{(p-1)/2} = -1+pb, so (-1+pb)^p ≡ -1 (mod p²)

