===========================================================================
UNIFIED THEOREM (proved for odd, conjectured for even):
===========================================================================

For n >= 3:

  v_2(T(n)) = { (n-1)/2                     if n is odd    [PROVED]
              { n/2 + v_2(c(n))              if n is even   [CONJECTURED]

where c(n) = #{odd k : 1 ≤ k < n/2, gcd(k,n) = 1}.

For even n = 2^a × m (m odd):
  c(n) = 2^{a-2} × φ(m)  if a ≥ 2
  c(n) = φ(m)/2           if a = 1

v_2(c(n)) counts the 2-adic content of the coprime partition count.

DEEP REASON: The excess for even n comes from CANCELLATION at the
minimum v_2 level. There are c(n) terms with coprime 2-part partitions,
each contributing an ODD coefficient (since n_odd/(ab) is odd for odd a,b).
Their sum has v_2 = v_2(c(n)) by the 'sum of c odd numbers' principle.
